, "result_digest": "33dca58bb2cf8d9f", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"out\", \"n_neighbors\": 21, \"neighbors\": [10, 104, 153, 348, 585, 599, 733, 776, 873, 874, 1014, 1135, 1200, 1211, 1220, 1240, 1288, 1346, 1504, 1897, 1904], \"node\": 547, \"window\": [57000, 68051]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 34494, "tokens_after": 34494, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_14", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 294, "direction": "in", "window": [39251, 68051]}, "result_digest": "901e486a12fd8959", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"in\", \"n_neighbors\": 5, \"neighbors\": [92, 258, 687, 716, 790], \"node\": 294, \"window\": [39251, 68051]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 43091, "tokens_after": 43091, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_15", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 318, "direction": "in", "window": [39251, 68051]}, "result_digest": "490b09936a525146", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"in\", \"n_neighbors\": 2, \"neighbors\": [298, 1796], \"node\": 318, \"window\": [39251, 68051]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 43091, "tokens_after": 43091, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 450, "direction": "in", "window": [39251, 68051]}, "result_digest": "d6cbda9901dc5278", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"in\", \"n_neighbors\": 5, \"neighbors\": [384, 976, 1524, 1577, 1584], \"node\": 450, \"window\": [39251, 68051]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 43091, "tokens_after": 43091, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_b1e97ee9", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [547, 641], "window": [39251, 77651], "confidence": 0.79, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Both nodes are individually busy (547: 70 events, 641: 68 events, step_02) and are connected in the time-ignoring 2-hop neighbourhood (step_05), but the temporal profiles are anti-aligned. 641's incoming traffic is front-loaded (37 events in 39251-44051, decaying to 0 after 68051; steps 07/09), whereas 547's outgoing traffic only ramps up late (1-2 events per early bin, 26 events in the final bin 72851-77651; steps 06/08). Any influence path must therefore terminate before ~68051, yet in [39251,57000] node 547 contacts only {64, 977, 1458} (step_10) \u2014 none of which are 641's in-neighbours (step_04). The only contacts reaching 641 in the late feasible window [57000,68051] are 294, 318, 450, 941 (step_12), and their own in-neighbours (steps 14-16: {92,258,687,716,790}, {298,1796}, {384,976,1524,1577,1584}) contain neither 547 nor any of 547's 21 out-neighbours in that window (step_13). 641 also emits to only one node (1777, step_11), so it is essentially a sink. No chain of interactions with successive gaps <= 600 can carry influence from 547 to 641; the apparent connectivity is a static-graph artefact of two independently popular but temporally disjoint hubs."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_b1e97ee9\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [547, 641],\n  \"window\": [39251, 77651],\n  \"confidence\": 0.79,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Both nodes are individually busy (547: 70 events, 641: 68 events, step_02) and are connected in the time-ignoring 2-hop neighbourhood (step_05), but the temporal profiles are anti-aligned. 641's incoming traffic is front-loaded (37 events in 39251-44051, decaying to 0 after 68051; steps 07/09), whereas 547's outgoing traffic only ramps up late (1-2 events per early bin, 26 events in the final bin 72851-77651; steps 06/08). Any influence path must therefore terminate before ~68051, yet in [39251,57000] node 547 contacts only {64, 977, 1458} (step_10) \u2014 none of which are 641's in-neighbours (step_04). The only contacts reaching 641 in the late feasible window [57000,68051] are 294, 318, 450, 941 (step_12), and their own in-neighbours (steps 14-16: {92,258,687,716,790}, {298,1796}, {384,976,1524,1577,1584}) contain neither 547 nor any of 547's 21 out-neighbours in that window (step_13). 641 also emits to only one node (1777, step_11), so it is essentially a sink. No chain of interactions with successive gaps <= 600 can carry influence from 547 to 641; the apparent connectivity is a static-graph artefact of two independently popular but temporally disjoint hubs.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 52382, "total_output_tokens": 8406, "total_tokens": 60788, "total_latency_ms": 113558, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}